1
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:36,047
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of

2
00:02:36,047 --> 00:02:41,787
the Grand Line. These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World. Now,

3
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:46,127
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

4
00:02:46,127 --> 00:02:49,827
sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

5
00:02:49,827 --> 00:02:53,827
I will be the king of the pirates!

6
00:02:53,827 --> 00:03:01,727
Reuniting after their training, Luffy and his crew continue on to the New World.

7
00:03:01,727 --> 00:03:06,267
The first stop is Fishman Island, where they find themselves pulled into a civil war.

8
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:09,647
After meeting with Jinbei, they learn of the events that led to their battle with the new

9
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:15,647
Fishman pirates. They also learn of Queen Otohime, who despite opposition, fought for understanding

10
00:03:15,647 --> 00:03:18,147
between humans and fishmen.

11
00:03:18,147 --> 00:03:19,147
Be careful, Mother.

12
00:03:19,147 --> 00:03:20,587
Don't go, Mother!

13
00:03:20,587 --> 00:03:21,587
Queen Otohime!

14
00:03:21,587 --> 00:03:24,587
What? I don't get it. Where is she going?

15
00:03:24,587 --> 00:03:27,587
My queen.

16
00:03:27,587 --> 00:03:33,587
Trust in me. Have faith in the woman you married, and the humans.

17
00:03:40,587 --> 00:03:42,587
Goodbye, Mother!

18
00:03:42,587 --> 00:03:44,587
I will miss you!

19
00:03:44,587 --> 00:03:46,587
Come home safe!

20
00:03:46,587 --> 00:03:50,587
You have missed me!

21
00:03:50,587 --> 00:03:54,587
Please be careful up there!

22
00:03:54,587 --> 00:03:57,587
I love you, Mother!

23
00:04:09,587 --> 00:04:12,587
A sudden tragedy! A gunshot shuts down the future!

24
00:04:12,587 --> 00:04:19,587
Queen Otohime's voyage would determine the fate of Fishman Island and its people.

25
00:04:19,587 --> 00:04:25,587
Of course, the uncertainty weighed heavily upon our shoulders. But for her family, it was

26
00:04:25,587 --> 00:04:28,587
even worse, I'm sure.

27
00:04:28,587 --> 00:04:33,587
Her children were restless, awaiting news of her safe return. In this, the island was united.

28
00:04:33,587 --> 00:04:43,587
Whether we were royalty or commoners, all we could do was pray for our queen.

29
00:04:43,587 --> 00:04:46,587
What? A magic box?

30
00:04:46,587 --> 00:04:50,587
Yep. In the palace. It's called the tomate box, to be exact.

31
00:04:50,587 --> 00:04:53,587
And it has the power to make you suddenly grow older?

32
00:04:53,587 --> 00:04:55,587
Yep. Well, that's what they say at least.

33
00:04:55,587 --> 00:05:03,587
So that means, if a kiddo like the princess opened it, then BAM! She'd be a full grown sexy babe lickety split?

34
00:05:03,587 --> 00:05:05,587
That would be the idea, sir.

35
00:05:05,587 --> 00:05:13,587
Problem solved! That is just what I need! Now I can get married to Shirahoshi right away and it won't be creepy! Or so I suspect.

36
00:05:13,587 --> 00:05:23,587
Now! Go and steal that magic box thing and steal it quick! No, wait. That gate at the palace is gonna stop us for sure, huh?

37
00:05:23,587 --> 00:05:26,587
I say you just marry her first and work out the details later.

38
00:05:26,587 --> 00:05:28,587
Yeah, everybody knows you're a creed.

39
00:05:28,587 --> 00:05:38,587
Whoa! Now there's an idea! Shirahoshi is pretty cute already. Even if the box thing doesn't work out, if I give it ten years or so, she'll be a knockout.

40
00:05:38,587 --> 00:05:40,587
Yeah, but she's gonna get even bigger, you know.

41
00:05:40,587 --> 00:05:45,587
Hey! Different strokes for different folks, buddy! I happen to like big women just fine!

42
00:05:45,587 --> 00:05:51,587
Not to mention, she can control the Sea King so her powers are big too! As big as my ambitions!

43
00:05:51,587 --> 00:05:57,587
She just needs the right man in her life! And we'll have the whole world in the palm of our hands!

44
00:05:57,587 --> 00:06:04,587
That means money, money, money, money! I'm telling you it's my destiny! The dream of every decade sets the beginning of time!

45
00:06:04,587 --> 00:06:09,587
Now, let's get started on writing those wedding invitations, shall we?

46
00:06:09,587 --> 00:06:12,587
You have to propose to her first!

47
00:06:12,587 --> 00:06:15,587
Wait! I don't have any friends!

48
00:06:15,587 --> 00:06:21,587
Days passed with no word from the Queen. The hearts of her people grew heavy.

49
00:06:21,587 --> 00:06:24,587
I really miss hearing her speeches.

50
00:06:24,587 --> 00:06:29,587
Please return safely, Queen Otohime!

51
00:06:29,587 --> 00:06:33,587
Boss? What's wrong? Why isn't she back?

52
00:06:33,587 --> 00:06:35,587
You think something bad happened?

53
00:06:35,587 --> 00:06:41,587
Keep the faith. She is fighting to protect your future, children. This island's future.

54
00:06:41,587 --> 00:06:46,587
Our hearts are with you, Your Majesty.

55
00:06:46,587 --> 00:06:51,587
Please come home!

56
00:06:51,587 --> 00:07:08,587
Worry not, my children. Your mother is a strong and wise woman.

57
00:07:08,587 --> 00:07:09,587
Wise woman.

58
00:07:11,587 --> 00:07:14,587
Although it was but a week, it felt like an eternity.

59
00:07:17,587 --> 00:07:19,587
Then, at long last...

60
00:07:19,587 --> 00:07:20,587
Hm?

61
00:07:20,587 --> 00:07:33,587
Finally!

62
00:07:33,587 --> 00:07:34,587
She's back! Your Majesty!

63
00:07:34,587 --> 00:07:38,587
She's back! Your Majesty!

64
00:07:38,587 --> 00:07:48,587
I was so worried!

65
00:07:48,587 --> 00:07:53,587
I'm not crying, I just have something in my eyes.

66
00:07:53,587 --> 00:07:57,587
She's back!

67
00:07:57,587 --> 00:08:01,587
Your Majesty!

68
00:08:01,587 --> 00:08:05,587
I was so worried!

69
00:08:05,587 --> 00:08:09,587
I'm not crying, I just have something in my eye!

70
00:08:09,587 --> 00:08:13,587
Welcome home! Your Majesty!

71
00:08:13,587 --> 00:08:17,587
After several days of negotiations, Queen Otohime was able to

72
00:08:17,587 --> 00:08:21,587
quell the fury of the Celestial Dragons. And perhaps more importantly,

73
00:08:21,587 --> 00:08:25,587
she brought a piece of paper back with her that would prove a beacon of hope to our entire

74
00:08:25,587 --> 00:08:29,587
island. In truth, it was a greater miracle than any of us could have imagined.

75
00:08:29,587 --> 00:08:33,587
Everyone, despite our troubled history with them, the Celestial Dragons

76
00:08:33,587 --> 00:08:37,587
are very influential. And by meeting with them, I have been able

77
00:08:37,587 --> 00:08:41,587
to bridge a gap. We may attend the World Summit

78
00:08:41,587 --> 00:08:45,587
yet. Listen to what they've written to improve humankind's

79
00:08:45,587 --> 00:08:49,587
relationship with fishmen. We give this petition written by

80
00:08:49,587 --> 00:08:53,587
their Queen. Our full endorsement.

81
00:08:53,587 --> 00:08:55,587
In other words, if we can fill my petition with

82
00:08:55,587 --> 00:08:57,587
signatures, the World Leaders at the Summit

83
00:08:57,587 --> 00:08:59,587
will have no choice but to recognize our

84
00:08:59,587 --> 00:09:01,587
right to be there. And furthermore,

85
00:09:01,587 --> 00:09:03,587
our right to be a part of the surface world.

86
00:09:03,587 --> 00:09:05,587
Finally, we will see our dream!

87
00:09:05,587 --> 00:09:09,587
I have mixed feelings about getting support from those guys.

88
00:09:09,587 --> 00:09:11,587
I'm still not sure.

89
00:09:11,587 --> 00:09:15,587
And now, it's in your hands. We still need more signatures.

90
00:09:15,587 --> 00:09:19,587
I have found the way, but this is a path we must walk together.

91
00:09:19,587 --> 00:09:23,587
Please, let your cry for freedom be heard.

92
00:09:23,587 --> 00:09:27,587
Only then, can we live above among our human friends.

93
00:09:27,587 --> 00:09:41,587
We've come so far! Please! Your signatures can change our future!

94
00:09:41,587 --> 00:09:59,587
Thank you, bud. Don't get my hopes up. If you're just going to change your mind again...

95
00:09:59,587 --> 00:10:03,587
We won't! My mom said she's gonna sign too!

96
00:10:03,587 --> 00:10:17,587
Unh...

97
00:10:17,587 --> 00:10:22,587
Toro Lunci

98
00:10:22,587 --> 00:10:27,587
Ha...

99
00:10:27,587 --> 00:10:45,127
No offense, Majesty, but I think you're going to need a much bigger box.

100
00:10:45,507 --> 00:10:48,367
And you better hurry, because the whole country's going to be lining up.

101
00:10:50,687 --> 00:10:53,507
Don't worry, Your Highness. I had a feeling this might happen.

102
00:10:53,507 --> 00:10:58,047
Those of you who support our Queen, put your signatures in here, please!

103
00:10:58,047 --> 00:11:26,427
There's only so much we can do by ignoring our prejudice.

104
00:11:26,427 --> 00:11:29,267
We need someone like her to take a step forward.

105
00:11:30,407 --> 00:11:36,447
We can denounce hate, but to instill hope is a far greater gift.

106
00:11:37,347 --> 00:11:40,687
This is our future-given life, sooner than we ever imagined.

107
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:44,507
She can transform this island more than a life of fighting ever could.

108
00:11:45,467 --> 00:11:49,187
I wish that Arlong understood that to save him from hatred.

109
00:11:49,187 --> 00:11:53,067
I wonder, what will he think of our future?

110
00:11:55,087 --> 00:11:59,627
I wish Tiger were here. Surely this would have warmed his heart.

111
00:12:05,407 --> 00:12:08,987
Mother, signatures keep pouring in from all over the country!

112
00:12:09,547 --> 00:12:11,227
Things seem to be progressing well.

113
00:12:11,567 --> 00:12:12,847
It's a dream come true.

114
00:12:12,847 --> 00:12:14,867
Yeah, and your courage made it come true!

115
00:12:16,267 --> 00:12:17,687
Well, I...

116
00:12:17,687 --> 00:12:19,967
did feel some inspiration.

117
00:12:20,727 --> 00:12:23,827
I felt as if a new road had been paved for the future of our people,

118
00:12:24,067 --> 00:12:25,547
when that miracle happened.

119
00:12:26,087 --> 00:12:26,567
Miracle?

120
00:12:28,147 --> 00:12:28,627
Yes.

121
00:12:29,147 --> 00:12:31,667
What else could you call the appearance of those Sea Kings?

122
00:12:32,627 --> 00:12:33,767
That was nuts!

123
00:12:33,907 --> 00:12:34,827
Think they like us?

124
00:12:35,767 --> 00:12:36,207
No.

125
00:12:37,027 --> 00:12:38,267
Shirahoshi called them here.

126
00:12:38,267 --> 00:12:40,627
I don't think it's so strange.

127
00:12:41,267 --> 00:12:43,167
After all, we can speak to fish, can't we?

128
00:12:43,767 --> 00:12:45,647
That's part of what it means to be merfolk.

129
00:12:46,967 --> 00:12:49,707
And yet, whenever we try to communicate with the great Sea Kings,

130
00:12:49,987 --> 00:12:52,367
for whatever reason, our words fall on deaf ears.

131
00:12:53,587 --> 00:12:56,707
No one on Fishman Island can speak to whales except for your father.

132
00:12:56,947 --> 00:12:59,847
But the Sea Kings, well, they're beyond even him.

133
00:13:00,607 --> 00:13:03,267
They say, in a legend passed down by our family,

134
00:13:03,267 --> 00:13:05,787
that every few hundred years,

135
00:13:06,287 --> 00:13:08,387
a mermaid will be born into the royal house

136
00:13:08,387 --> 00:13:11,827
with a fearsome power that no one else on the island possesses.

137
00:13:11,987 --> 00:13:13,647
The power to talk to Sea Kings?

138
00:13:14,107 --> 00:13:15,547
And Shirahoshi is the one?

139
00:13:16,267 --> 00:13:17,707
I believe she is.

140
00:13:18,187 --> 00:13:19,887
And according to the rest of the legend,

141
00:13:20,267 --> 00:13:22,787
she will meet someone who will guide both her and her power

142
00:13:22,787 --> 00:13:24,967
in a direction that will change the world.

143
00:13:24,967 --> 00:13:27,987
I can't wait to see.

144
00:13:28,447 --> 00:13:29,427
Oh, wow!

145
00:13:29,747 --> 00:13:31,667
Of course, if the world does change,

146
00:13:31,967 --> 00:13:34,667
then that will likely mean a change to this island as well.

147
00:13:34,687 --> 00:13:35,027
Yeah?

148
00:13:35,307 --> 00:13:37,727
You think it'll help with the world's summit thing you're doing?

149
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:38,587
Perhaps.

150
00:13:39,347 --> 00:13:40,827
For if it is used with love,

151
00:13:41,167 --> 00:13:43,087
her power could save thousands of lives.

152
00:13:43,627 --> 00:13:44,647
That is my hope.

153
00:13:45,527 --> 00:13:46,447
But who can say?

154
00:13:47,007 --> 00:13:49,447
It may be darkness that will rule her heart instead.

155
00:13:49,927 --> 00:13:52,747
In that case, her power could sink the world.

156
00:13:52,747 --> 00:13:56,487
Of course, Shirahoshi is just a child.

157
00:13:56,947 --> 00:13:58,647
I'm sure she has no such intentions.

158
00:13:59,327 --> 00:14:00,767
But because she is a child,

159
00:14:01,147 --> 00:14:02,887
she has yet to understand her power

160
00:14:02,887 --> 00:14:04,407
and cannot control it.

161
00:14:04,827 --> 00:14:06,607
If something traumatic were to happen to her,

162
00:14:06,947 --> 00:14:09,507
she could unwittingly cause the Sea Kings to go berserk

163
00:14:09,507 --> 00:14:10,867
and in great numbers.

164
00:14:11,487 --> 00:14:11,887
What?

165
00:14:12,067 --> 00:14:14,987
Then our whole island would be smashed into itty-bitty bits!

166
00:14:15,327 --> 00:14:16,687
What the heck should we do?

167
00:14:16,727 --> 00:14:17,227
Don't worry.

168
00:14:17,607 --> 00:14:20,127
You can count on me to take care of her for the time being.

169
00:14:20,127 --> 00:14:23,107
Although, one of these days,

170
00:14:23,227 --> 00:14:24,987
the three of you must become warriors,

171
00:14:25,387 --> 00:14:26,327
brave and true.

172
00:14:27,087 --> 00:14:29,887
Then, as warriors and brothers alike,

173
00:14:30,227 --> 00:14:31,287
use your strength

174
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:34,267
to protect your sister no matter what.

175
00:14:34,807 --> 00:14:35,207
Yeah!

176
00:14:35,567 --> 00:14:36,307
But of course!

177
00:14:37,027 --> 00:14:37,847
Thank you.

178
00:14:39,527 --> 00:14:41,527
But even as they made that vow,

179
00:14:41,627 --> 00:14:44,127
they could not have expected what would come next.

180
00:14:44,127 --> 00:15:03,727
Signatures for the petition were mounting at a rapid pace.

181
00:15:04,567 --> 00:15:06,967
The islanders were still distrustful of humans.

182
00:15:06,967 --> 00:15:11,547
But they longed to see the beginning of a new era all the same.

183
00:15:12,227 --> 00:15:13,847
Hey, Queen Ojohime!

184
00:15:14,687 --> 00:15:17,187
We signed papers again so you can have more!

185
00:15:17,387 --> 00:15:18,707
That's against the rules.

186
00:15:19,027 --> 00:15:21,167
Each person can only vote one time.

187
00:15:21,347 --> 00:15:21,707
Ugh!

188
00:15:22,427 --> 00:15:23,627
We're sorry.

189
00:15:24,127 --> 00:15:24,847
It's okay.

190
00:15:25,547 --> 00:15:27,007
Even if I can't accept them,

191
00:15:27,107 --> 00:15:28,447
it's the thought that counts, right?

192
00:15:28,947 --> 00:15:29,707
Thank you.

193
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:31,407
I mean it.

194
00:15:31,407 --> 00:15:34,787
It seems her persistence is finally paying off.

195
00:15:50,627 --> 00:15:51,507
Get away!

196
00:15:51,727 --> 00:15:52,147
Fire!

197
00:15:52,387 --> 00:15:52,767
Fire!

198
00:15:53,427 --> 00:15:54,547
Are we under attack?

199
00:15:54,667 --> 00:15:55,427
What's going on?

200
00:15:55,507 --> 00:15:55,847
Water!

201
00:15:56,127 --> 00:15:56,687
Get water!

202
00:15:56,847 --> 00:15:57,067
Quick!

203
00:15:57,227 --> 00:15:57,747
Put it out!

204
00:15:58,187 --> 00:15:59,467
Who would do such a thing?

205
00:15:59,467 --> 00:16:01,607
We'll lose all of the signatures at this rate!

206
00:16:01,647 --> 00:16:01,927
Hurry!

207
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:02,707
Run away!

208
00:16:04,127 --> 00:16:04,567
Wait!

209
00:16:05,127 --> 00:16:06,267
Your Highness, no!

210
00:16:06,387 --> 00:16:07,247
It's not too late!

211
00:16:07,527 --> 00:16:08,807
Save whatever you can!

212
00:16:09,707 --> 00:16:10,827
You can't do this!

213
00:16:10,867 --> 00:16:11,547
It's too dangerous!

214
00:16:11,567 --> 00:16:14,367
I didn't make it this far just to lie down and give up!

215
00:16:15,607 --> 00:16:16,387
Be careful!

216
00:16:17,487 --> 00:16:19,727
I will protect them to my last breath!

217
00:16:20,227 --> 00:16:21,327
These aren't just papers!

218
00:16:21,727 --> 00:16:22,687
This is our future!

219
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:25,907
We can't let the future of our island go up in flames!

220
00:16:26,827 --> 00:16:27,607
Yes, ma'am.

221
00:16:27,607 --> 00:16:29,787
Save any papers you can!

222
00:16:30,047 --> 00:16:30,527
Yes, sir!

223
00:16:30,847 --> 00:16:31,687
Retreat to safety.

224
00:16:32,107 --> 00:16:33,347
You can count on us.

225
00:16:33,347 --> 00:16:33,467
Yes, sir!

226
00:16:57,607 --> 00:17:15,247
Queen Otohime has been shot!

227
00:17:16,107 --> 00:17:17,427
Someone find the shooter!

228
00:17:17,627 --> 00:17:18,907
Don't let the culprit escape!

229
00:17:19,027 --> 00:17:19,567
We'll help!

230
00:17:20,027 --> 00:17:21,267
Guard the royal vandler!

231
00:17:21,447 --> 00:17:22,347
Mother, no!

232
00:17:22,487 --> 00:17:22,907
Mother!

233
00:17:22,907 --> 00:17:24,607
It's too dangerous here!

234
00:17:24,767 --> 00:17:26,067
Get on the gondola and quickly!

235
00:17:26,507 --> 00:17:27,067
Move!

236
00:17:27,127 --> 00:17:27,867
Don't go!

237
00:17:28,867 --> 00:17:31,067
Your Majesty, answer me!

238
00:17:32,067 --> 00:17:32,767
Who would tell this?

239
00:17:32,767 --> 00:17:33,287
Otohime!

240
00:17:35,367 --> 00:17:37,327
Oh, what a shame!

241
00:17:37,607 --> 00:17:38,847
Well, don't mind me.

242
00:17:38,947 --> 00:17:40,587
Nothing suspicious going on here.

243
00:17:40,687 --> 00:17:41,307
Who are you?

244
00:17:41,467 --> 00:17:42,127
No one!

245
00:17:42,647 --> 00:17:44,307
Stay away from the princess!

246
00:17:44,727 --> 00:17:44,907
Hey!

247
00:17:45,127 --> 00:17:45,687
Stop!

248
00:17:45,687 --> 00:17:49,327
Please, someone tell me she's all right!

249
00:17:49,447 --> 00:17:50,167
Say something!

250
00:17:51,127 --> 00:17:51,427
No!

251
00:17:51,747 --> 00:17:52,787
It can't be!

252
00:17:57,827 --> 00:17:58,467
Dammit!

253
00:17:58,687 --> 00:18:00,047
No one do such a thing!

254
00:18:00,107 --> 00:18:00,987
We need a doctor!

255
00:18:01,147 --> 00:18:02,307
What's taking so long?

256
00:18:02,367 --> 00:18:03,067
Oh, please!

257
00:18:03,287 --> 00:18:04,067
Answer me, Mother!

258
00:18:04,087 --> 00:18:05,467
Come on, open your eyes!

259
00:18:05,527 --> 00:18:07,787
Whoever did this, I'll make them pay!

260
00:18:07,787 --> 00:18:07,827
I'll make them pay!

261
00:18:07,827 --> 00:18:13,627
